<title>USA: Nevada Energy sued by former directors.</title>
<headline>Nevada Energy sued by former directors.</headline>
<byline>Rita Farrell</byline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two former directors of Nevada Energy Co have sued the company's new president and board, alleging that they misappropriated assets after taking control of Nevada in May.</p>
<p>In a complaint filed Thursday in the Delaware Chancery Court and made available to Reuters Monday, plaintiffs Michael Kassouff and Richard Cascarilla, also a former officer, claim the alleged misappropriation began when the Irish corporation Waterford Trust took control of Nevada in return for $5 million in equity financing.</p>
</text>
